## Decision batch

The cells marked undecided wait for the maintainer (carve#5658). Until they are ruled the test does not assert them.

- D1: a refused `+` right after a refused brace run (row R03). CARVE-P2-035 keeps the line after the run in the paragraph; §17 L3 makes a lone `+` at the marker column a marker that renders nothing.
- D2: an own-line `+` fence, a blank, then a fence line one column right of the marker column (row F06). carve#5587 gives one closer test per host for a marker-line `+`; carve#5560 reads an own-line `+` fence like a fence in the host's body.

## Known model gaps

The test lists the cells where the spec model still renders another owner than this table, each with the ticket that tracks it: carve#5639 (a refused `+` after a blank in a note or description that an own-line `+` opened), carve#5635 (an own-line `+` fence in a list item keeps its blank), and two shapes first measured by this table, both on carve#5658: a shifted closer after the blank in a note or description fence (row F05), and an attribute run in a quote followed by an unmarked line (rows Q01 and Q03).
